//	and every range must lie wholly inside them: otherwise
//	CAMPAIGN_WINDOW_OUTSIDE_LIMIT, on create and on every change. Ranges of one
//	window may not overlap. A closed window does not pause the campaign.
//	maxConcurrent: Optional `integer` value serialized in the `maxConcurrent`
//	wire field.
//	ringTimeoutSec: At least 5 and strictly below the 60-second answer window,
//	else CAMPAIGN_RING_TIMEOUT_TOO_LONG. Absent keeps the stored value.
//	retryPolicy: A retry policy as a client writes it. The object sent is the
//	whole policy: a field left out takes its default (never the stored value),
//	and an interval left out of intervalSec takes its default. The default
//	retries every retryable outcome.
//	defaultCountryCode: Optional `string` value serialized in the
//	`defaultCountryCode` wire field.
//	followUpQueueId: Optional `uuid`-formatted value serialized in the
//	`followUpQueueId` wire field.
func (sdk *CampaignsNamespace) Update(ctx context.Context, params UpdateCampaignParams, opts ...RequestOption) (*Campaign, error) {
	return UpdateCampaign(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}

// Delete delete a draft campaign
//
// Only a DRAFT can be deleted, with its contacts. A campaign that has started is history: cancel it instead. Any other status is 409 CAMPAIGN_INVALID_TRANSITION. Needs campaigns:write.
func (sdk *CampaignsNamespace) Delete(ctx context.Context, params DeleteCampaignParams, opts ...RequestOption) (any, error) {
	return DeleteCampaign(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}

// Start start a campaign
//
// DRAFT to RUNNING. The campaign is checked once more first (its DID, flow and window may have changed since it was written; the outer calling hours may have been narrowed), and every ACTIVE contact becomes due. Any other status is 409 CAMPAIGN_INVALID_TRANSITION. Racing requests are decided by the database: of two simultaneous starts, or a start and a cancel, exactly one wins and the other is 409. Needs campaigns:write. A deployment that cannot place an outbound call at all (`AICC_OUTBOUND_ENDPOINT` empty: the value that renders a number into the trunk's dial string) answers 409 OUTBOUND_NOT_CONFIGURED and writes no attempt, rather than starting a campaign whose every attempt would fail and be retried for hours. `deploy/carrier.md` says how to set it.
func (sdk *CampaignsNamespace) Start(ctx context.Context, params StartCampaignParams, opts ...RequestOption) (*Campaign, error) {
	return StartCampaign(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}

// Pause pause a campaign
//
// RUNNING to PAUSED with pauseReason MANUAL. New calls stop; calls in flight finish. Any other status is 409 CAMPAIGN_INVALID_TRANSITION. Racing requests are decided by the database: of two simultaneous starts, or a start and a cancel, exactly one wins and the other is 409. Needs campaigns:write.
func (sdk *CampaignsNamespace) Pause(ctx context.Context, params PauseCampaignParams, opts ...RequestOption) (*Campaign, error) {
	return PauseCampaign(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}

// Resume resume a campaign
//
// PAUSED to RUNNING, whatever paused it, and the pause reason is cleared. Any other status is 409 CAMPAIGN_INVALID_TRANSITION. Racing requests are decided by the database: of two simultaneous starts, or a start and a cancel, exactly one wins and the other is 409. Needs campaigns:write. A deployment that cannot place an outbound call at all (`AICC_OUTBOUND_ENDPOINT` empty) answers 409 OUTBOUND_NOT_CONFIGURED and the campaign stays PAUSED, rather than reporting RUNNING a campaign the dialer would pause again on its first attempt. `deploy/carrier.md` says how to set it.
func (sdk *CampaignsNamespace) Resume(ctx context.Context, params ResumeCampaignParams, opts ...RequestOption) (*Campaign, error) {
	return ResumeCampaign(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}

// Cancel cancel a campaign
//
// DRAFT, RUNNING or PAUSED to CANCELLED, which is final. Calls in flight finish; contacts and leads stay readable. COMPLETED is not reachable through the API: the dialer completes a campaign when nothing is left to dial. Any other status is 409 CAMPAIGN_INVALID_TRANSITION. Racing requests are decided by the database: of two simultaneous starts, or a start and a cancel, exactly one wins and the other is 409. Needs campaigns:write.
func (sdk *CampaignsNamespace) Cancel(ctx context.Context, params CancelCampaignParams, opts ...RequestOption) (*Campaign, error) {
	return CancelCampaign(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}

// ListContacts list a campaign's contacts
//
// In import order. status and leadIntent narrow the list. Needs campaigns:read.
func (sdk *CampaignsNamespace) ListContacts(ctx context.Context, params ListCampaignContactsParams, opts ...RequestOption) (*CampaignContactList, error) {
	return ListCampaignContacts(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}

// ImportContacts import contacts
//
// Adds a list of contacts, at most 5000 per request (more is 422 VALIDATION_FAILED, params {field: "contacts", rule: TOO_MANY_ROWS}; send the list in several requests). The body is the only thing that can fail the request: a row that cannot be used is rejected on its own with a code, and never fails the others. The good rows are stored in one transaction. The answer has one result per request row, in request order: IMPORTED (contactId is the new contact), DUPLICATE (contactId is the contact that already had the number: the first one wins and its slots are not overwritten; a number repeated inside the request is a duplicate of its first row) or REJECTED with a code (NUMBER_EMPTY, NUMBER_INVALID, TIME_ZONE_INVALID, SLOTS_TOO_MANY, SLOT_UNKNOWN, SLOT_TOO_LONG). A slot the flow does not read is SLOT_UNKNOWN, so a column maps only to a name in the campaign's read-only flowFields. Numbers are canonicalised to E.164 with the campaign's defaultCountryCode, else the deployment's AICC_DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE, so "+8613800138000" and "138 0013 8000" are one contact. The same number in two campaigns is a contact in each. Importing again what was imported before is all DUPLICATE. The do-not-call list is not consulted here: the dialer checks it before every call, so a number added to it later still stops. Allowed in DRAFT, RUNNING and PAUSED; a COMPLETED or CANCELLED campaign answers 409 CAMPAIGN_INVALID_TRANSITION. Contacts added to a RUNNING or PAUSED campaign are due at once. Needs campaigns:write.
//
// Parameters:
//
//	contacts: Required array value serialized in the `contacts` wire field.
func (sdk *CampaignsNamespace) ImportContacts(ctx context.Context, params ImportCampaignContactsParams, opts ...RequestOption) (*CampaignImportResult, error) {
	return ImportCampaignContacts(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}

// ListAttempts list a campaign's attempts
//
// Newest first. contactId and outcome narrow the list. Needs campaigns:read.
func (sdk *CampaignsNamespace) ListAttempts(ctx context.Context, params ListCampaignAttemptsParams, opts ...RequestOption) (*CampaignAttemptList, error) {
	return ListCampaignAttempts(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}

